 ['Footprints beneath the window','Fresh tracks lead nowhere in the storm. Dr. Arbuthnot questions the investigator’s assumptions; a railway attendant fears that a small mistake will condemn them all.','Does a neat explanation deserve trust if it depends on silencing someone?',[['As the attendant, describe exactly what you saw','Stand by your account','confidence','You made a modest observation part of the larger truth.'],['As Arbuthnot, challenge the theory without hiding your own stake','Practice accountable skepticism','integrity','You asked hard questions while accepting that your own motives mattered too.']]],
